          <attvalue for="7" value="PI3K" />
          <attvalue for="8" value="competitive_inhibition" />
          <attvalue for="9" value="inhibits" />
          <attvalue for="10" value="Class I PI3K inhibition lowers PIP3 and therefore both AKT recruitment and mSin1-dependent mTORC2 activation. In a randomised comparison with everolimus in renal cell carcinoma, apitolisib produced shorter progression-free survival and markedly more high-grade hyperglycaemia and rash, illustrating the toxicity ceiling that limited dual PI3K-mTOR inhibitors developed to pre-empt feedback reactivation." />
