          <attvalue for="10" value="mTORC1 drives the adaptive growth of cardiomyocytes, so partial inhibition blunts physiological hypertrophy; the same inhibition attenuates pathological hypertrophy in multiple models and regresses established pressure-overload hypertrophy, so the adaptive and maladaptive arms are not separable pharmacologically." />
