          <attvalue for="10" value="Glutaminase hydrolyses glutamine to glutamate and ammonia, the first step of glutaminolysis; glutamate is then converted to alpha-ketoglutarate by GLUD1 or transaminases, so GLS is required for, but does not itself produce, alpha-ketoglutarate from glutamine." />
