          <attvalue for="8" value="other" />
          <attvalue for="9" value="activates" />
          <attvalue for="10" value="Without FLCN GAP activity RagC/D remains GTP-bound, so mTORC1 cannot phosphorylate TFEB at Ser211 even though it phosphorylates S6K1 and 4E-BP1 normally, and TFEB accumulates constitutively in the nucleus; removing TFEB rescues the renal phenotype of kidney-specific Flcn-knockout mice, indicating that this substrate-selective lesion rather than global mTORC1 hyperactivity drives it." />
