          <attvalue for="9" value="inhibits" />
          <attvalue for="10" value="AKT phosphorylates TSC2 at five sites, Ser939 and Thr1462 being dominant, creating 14-3-3 binding sites; the demonstrated consequence is release of the TSC complex from the lysosomal membrane where Rheb resides, so Rheb·GTP accumulates. Stable dissociation of TSC1 from TSC2 remains poorly supported." />
