          <attvalue for="9" value="required_for" />
          <attvalue for="10" value="mTOR signalling is required for oligodendrocyte differentiation and myelination. Loss of Raptor delays the onset of myelination, reduces sheath thickness and impairs differentiation in a region-dependent manner, most severely in spinal cord, whereas loss of Rictor has modest effects and combined loss is most severe, so mTORC1 is dominant and mTORC2 contributory." />
