          <attvalue for="8" value="physiological_output" />
          <attvalue for="9" value="modulates" />
          <attvalue for="10" value="The role of mTOR in osteoclast differentiation is unsettled: rapamycin suppresses RANKL-driven osteoclastogenesis in culture, whereas deletion of Raptor in osteoclast precursors has been reported to enhance differentiation and low-dose rapamycin can increase bone resorption in vivo. The net skeletal effect of inhibition is therefore context-dependent and not predictable from cell-autonomous data." />
